.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH bbcli 1  "bbcli " 
.SH NAME
bbcli \- BarterBackup CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B Usage:
Usage: bbcli [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
BarterBackup CLI
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-\-local\-addr <LOCAL_ADDR>"
local_addr is the local daemon endpoint
.RS
env: BBCLI_LOCAL_ADDR
.RE
.TP
.B "\-\-data\-dir <DATA_DIR>"
data_dir is the base directory for daemon state and local CLI keys
.RS
env: BBCLI_DATA_DIR
.RE
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B "bbcli state"
Print daemon state
.TP
.B "bbcli init"
Initialize daemon storage with the main password or complete one recovery\-mode initialization
.TP
.B "bbcli unlock"
Send the main password to the daemon unlock path
.TP
.B "bbcli stop"
Ask the daemon to shut down gracefully
.TP
.B "bbcli peer"
Manage known peers
.TP
.B "bbcli file"
Manage files in the latest encrypted content blob
.TP
.B "bbcli config"
Read or update daemon configuration
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "bbcli state"
Print daemon state
.PP
.nf
.B Usage:
Usage: bbcli state
.fi
.SS "bbcli init"
Initialize daemon storage with the main password or complete one recovery\-mode initialization
.PP
.nf
.B Usage:
Usage: bbcli init [OPTIONS] [PASSWORD]
       init <COMMAND>
.fi
.PP
.B Options
.TP
.B "\-\-password\-stdin"
password_stdin reads the main password from standard input
.TP
.B "\-\-allow\-weak\-password"
allow_weak_password bypasses the local password\-strength gate
.TP
.B "\-\-wait\-seconds <WAIT_SECONDS>"
wait_seconds is how long to wait for daemon startup readiness
.RS
default: 30
.RE
.TP
.B "\-\-recovery\-mode"
recovery_mode blocks outgoing publication until recovery is finished
.TP
.B "password <PASSWORD>"
password is the inline main password or seed string
.PP
.B Subcommands
.TP
.B "bbcli init complete"
Complete recovery\-mode initialization and allow publication
.SS "bbcli init complete"
Complete recovery\-mode initialization and allow publication
.PP
.nf
.B Usage:
Usage: bbcli init complete
.fi
.SS "bbcli unlock"
Send the main password to the daemon unlock path
.PP
.nf
.B Usage:
Usage: bbcli unlock [OPTIONS] [PASSWORD]
.fi
.PP
.B Options
.TP
.B "\-\-password\-stdin"
password_stdin reads the main password from standard input
.TP
.B "\-\-wait\-seconds <WAIT_SECONDS>"
wait_seconds is how long to wait for daemon startup readiness
.RS
default: 30
.RE
.TP
.B "password <PASSWORD>"
password is the inline main password or seed string
.SS "bbcli stop"
Ask the daemon to shut down gracefully
.PP
.nf
.B Usage:
Usage: bbcli stop
.fi
.SS "bbcli peer"
Manage known peers
.PP
.nf
.B Usage:
Usage: bbcli peer <COMMAND>
.fi
.PP
.B Subcommands
.TP
.B "bbcli peer connect"
Add a peer onion identifier to the daemon's known peer list
.TP
.B "bbcli peer pin"
Pin a tracked peer so local policy treats it as operator\-protected
.TP
.B "bbcli peer unpin"
Remove an existing operator pin from a tracked peer
.TP
.B "bbcli peer list"
Print the daemon's current peer inventory
.TP
.B "bbcli peer check"
Check one peer's current copy of our latest local revision
.SS "bbcli peer connect"
Add a peer onion identifier to the daemon's known peer list
.PP
.nf
.B Usage:
Usage: bbcli peer connect <ONION_SERVICE_ID>
.fi
.PP
.B Options
.TP
.B "onion_service_id <ONION_SERVICE_ID>"
onion_service_id is the peer onion service identifier
.SS "bbcli peer pin"
Pin a tracked peer so local policy treats it as operator\-protected
.PP
.nf
.B Usage:
Usage: bbcli peer pin <ONION_SERVICE_ID>
.fi
.PP
.B Options
.TP
.B "onion_service_id <ONION_SERVICE_ID>"
onion_service_id is the peer onion service identifier
.SS "bbcli peer unpin"
Remove an existing operator pin from a tracked peer
.PP
.nf
.B Usage:
Usage: bbcli peer unpin <ONION_SERVICE_ID>
.fi
.PP
.B Options
.TP
.B "onion_service_id <ONION_SERVICE_ID>"
onion_service_id is the peer onion service identifier
.SS "bbcli peer list"
Print the daemon's current peer inventory
.PP
.nf
.B Usage:
Usage: bbcli peer list [OPTIONS]
.fi
.PP
.B Options
.TP
.B "\-\-status <STATUS>"
status filters peers by current local transport state
.TP
.B "\-\-with\-storage"
with_storage keeps only peers with persisted storage state
.TP
.B "\-\-without\-storage"
without_storage keeps only peers without persisted storage state
.SS "bbcli peer check"
Check one peer's current copy of our latest local revision
.PP
.nf
.B Usage:
Usage: bbcli peer check <ONION_SERVICE_ID>
.fi
.PP
.B Options
.TP
.B "onion_service_id <ONION_SERVICE_ID>"
onion_service_id is the peer onion service identifier
.SS "bbcli file"
Manage files in the latest encrypted content blob
.PP
.nf
.B Usage:
Usage: bbcli file <COMMAND>
.fi
.PP
.B Subcommands
.TP
.B "bbcli file list"
Print the names of all files in the latest encrypted content blob
.TP
.B "bbcli file set"
Add or replace a file in the latest encrypted content blob
.TP
.B "bbcli file get"
Download a file from the latest encrypted content blob
.TP
.B "bbcli file delete"
Delete a file from the latest encrypted content blob
.SS "bbcli file list"
Print the names of all files in the latest encrypted content blob
.PP
.nf
.B Usage:
Usage: bbcli file list
.fi
.SS "bbcli file set"
Add or replace a file in the latest encrypted content blob
.PP
.nf
.B Usage:
Usage: bbcli file set <NAME> [PATH]
.fi
.PP
.B Options
.TP
.B "name <NAME>"
name is the stable file name inside the encrypted content set
.TP
.B "path <PATH>"
path is the optional plaintext file path to upload.

When omitted or `\-`, `bbcli` reads the plaintext bytes from standard input instead.
.SS "bbcli file get"
Download a file from the latest encrypted content blob
.PP
.nf
.B Usage:
Usage: bbcli file get <NAME> [OUT]
.fi
.PP
.B Options
.TP
.B "name <NAME>"
name is the stable file name inside the encrypted content set
.TP
.B "out <OUT>"
out is the optional output path for the downloaded plaintext file
.SS "bbcli file delete"
Delete a file from the latest encrypted content blob
.PP
.nf
.B Usage:
Usage: bbcli file delete <NAME>
.fi
.PP
.B Options
.TP
.B "name <NAME>"
name is the stable file name inside the encrypted content set
.SS "bbcli config"
Read or update daemon configuration
.PP
.nf
.B Usage:
Usage: bbcli config <COMMAND>
.fi
.PP
.B Subcommands
.TP
.B "bbcli config get"
Print the current configuration and derived storage usage data
.TP
.B "bbcli config set"
Update one or more configuration fields
.SS "bbcli config get"
Print the current configuration and derived storage usage data
.PP
.nf
.B Usage:
Usage: bbcli config get [OPTIONS]
.fi
.PP
.B Options
.TP
.B "\-\-peers\-storage"
peers_storage prints only the peer\-storage budget field
.TP
.B "\-\-min\-replicas"
min_replicas prints only the minimum replica target field
.TP
.B "\-\-resource\-policy"
resource_policy prints only the current read\-only peer runtime limits
.SS "bbcli config set"
Update one or more configuration fields
.PP
.nf
.B Usage:
Usage: bbcli config set [OPTIONS]
.fi
.PP
.B Options
.TP
.B "\-\-peers\-storage <PEERS_STORAGE>"
peers_storage sets the total bytes allocated to peer storage
.TP
.B "\-\-min\-replicas <MIN_REPLICAS>"
min_replicas sets the minimum replica target for our content
